From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rve build fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riscv32: enable statx for fstat

On riscv32 with Linux 6.x kernel headers, __NR_fstat and __NR_fstat64
are not defined because RISC-V does not set __ARCH_WANT_TIME32_SYSCALLS,
causing the NR3264_fstat definitions to be excluded. The only available
stat mechanism is statx (syscall 291).

Enable __UCLIBC_HAVE_STATX__ so that fstat.c (and related files) use
the statx code path instead of falling through to an undefined symbol.
---
 libc/sysdeps/linux/riscv32/bits/uClibc_arch_features.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libc/sysdeps/linux/riscv32/bits/uClibc_arch_features.h b/libc/sysdeps/linux/riscv32/bits/uClibc_arch_features.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/libc/sysdeps/linux/riscv32/bits/uClibc_arch_features.h
+++ b/libc/sysdeps/linux/riscv32/bits/uClibc_arch_features.h
@@ -13,2 +13,2 @@
-/* does your target use statx */
-#undef __UCLIBC_HAVE_STATX__
+/* riscv32 with 6.x kernel headers has no __NR_fstat; must use statx */
+#define __UCLIBC_HAVE_STATX__
--
2.30.2
